          "number": 5,
          "letter": "E",
          "english": "Members of the geographically dispersed subculture that Levels is a part of call themselves \"digital nomads\". They are borderless, mostly self-employed remote workers who interact with cities in a way that's entirely different from a tourist, but still doesn't quite reach the status of resident. A relatively new phenomenon, there are no hard statistics on the prevalence of digital nomads or location independent workers. But thanks to the growing prevalence of freelance(自由职业的) livelihoods, a global sharing economy and numerous digital tools, the number of people who are able to live this life is growing quickly. And in a rapidly urbanising world, where a major city in Asia increasingly offers the same comforts as one in Europe, many people are reaching the realisation they don't need to stay in one place.",
          "chinese": "Levels所属的这一地理上分散的亚文化群体称自己为“数字游民”。他们不受国界限制，大多是自雇的远程工作者；他们与城市互动的方式与游客完全不同，却又没有完全达到居民的身份。这是一个相对较新的现象，目前没有关于数字游民或不受地点限制的工作者普及程度的确切统计数据。但得益于自由职业生计的日益普及、全球共享经济以及众多数字工具，能够过上这种生活的人数正在迅速增加。在一个快速城市化的世界里，亚洲的一座大城市越来越能提供与欧洲城市相同的舒适条件，许多人开始意识到，他们不必一直待在同一个地方。",
